+**Version diff**
+
+Models learn from every version of a spec, and code follows whichever its author read: Back-Channel Logout 1.0 errata set 1 made `exp` REQUIRED in §2.4, and the version before it has no `exp`. `diff` (`Store::diff`) lists the normative statements that differ between two pinned versions of one document, from the section and step chunks already stored, with no schema change. The design is `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-28-spec-version-diff-design.md`.
+
+- **Versions:** `to` defaults to the current version and `from` to the older version pinned last (the highest `source.id` that is not current), since the index records no publication dates; with `to` given, `from` defaults to the version pinned last before it, so a diff never runs backwards. Either is named by its hash, with or without `sha256:`, or as a pinned version (`doc@sha256:…`, the form errors and `older_versions` list). A document with no other version, or a hash that matches no version or several, is `UnknownVersion` with the pinned versions; a document the corpus lacks, by name or alias, `UnknownSource`; a section in neither version `NoSuchSection` with the nearest sections.
